{"uid":"364a9b687fef6862","name":"test_same_size_rewrite_of_the_leading_indexed_line_falls_back_exactly","fullName":"tests.test_hub_real_render_cap_whole_call#test_same_size_rewrite_of_the_leading_indexed_line_falls_back_exactly","historyId":"02caa006458747792ec3418b10c52017","time":{"start":1791925354932,"stop":1791925354990,"duration":58},"description":"Task cure-01-03 (PRD C.1/C.3, D.1, DoD 3-4): a checkpoint's own\n    STATE can be silently wrong even when the transcript's total byte\n    count never changes -- an in-place, same-length rewrite of exactly the\n    render index's own leading (`checkpoints[0]`) raw line changes what a\n    fresh render of it would produce, but nothing downstream of\n    `render_index.load_index` ever re-reads those particular bytes on its\n    own (`_prepend_covered`'s backward walk always seeds a segment's\n    render from the PRECEDING checkpoint's STORED state, and simply stops\n    once it reaches the very first one, never validating it against\n    anything). Before this task's cure, `ui_server.rendered_log_lines`\n    returned the stale 'beta' (the ORIGINAL, pre-rewrite content) on both\n    surfaces instead of 'alpha' (what the ACTUAL current bytes render) --\n    a wrong-but-plausible answer, never an exception, so nothing forced a\n    fallback. This pins the cured contract: the index is refused outright\n    (`render_index.load_index`/`bounded_tail` -> `None`) and both surfaces\n    fall back to the exact full-render tail instead.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-03 (PRD C.1/C.3, D.1, DoD 3-4): a checkpoint's own<br />\nSTATE can be silently wrong even when the transcript's total byte<br />\ncount never changes -- an in-place, same-length rewrite of exactly the<br />\nrender index's own leading (<code>checkpoints[0]</code>) raw line changes what a<br />\nfresh render of it would produce, but nothing downstream of<br />\n<code>render_index.load_index</code> ever re-reads those particular bytes on its<br />\nown (<code>_prepend_covered</code>'s backward walk always seeds a segment's<br />\nrender from the PRECEDING checkpoint's STORED state, and simply stops<br />\nonce it reaches the very first one, never validating it against<br />\nanything). Before this task's cure, <code>ui_server.rendered_log_lines</code><br />\nreturned the stale 'beta' (the ORIGINAL, pre-rewrite content) on both<br />\nsurfaces instead of 'alpha' (what the ACTUAL current bytes render) --<br />\na wrong-but-plausible answer, never an exception, so nothing forced a<br />\nfallback. This pins the cured contract: the index is refused outright<br />\n(<code>render_index.load_index</code>/<code>bounded_tail</code> -&gt; <code>None</code>) and both surfaces<br />\nfall back to the exact full-render tail instead.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791925216481,"stop":1791925216481,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791925216482,"stop":1791925216482,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791925354918,"stop":1791925354922,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791925354918,"stop":1791925354918,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_s